<title>USA: BTG stake cut by Vinik group to 4.9 pct.</title>
<headline>BTG stake cut by Vinik group to 4.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by former Fidelity Magellan Fund manager Jeffrey Vinik said Tuesday it cut its stake in BTG Inc to 413,700 common shares or 4.9 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold shares between March 18 and April 15 at $17.99 to $19.63 each.</p>
<p>BTG, based in Vienna, Va., is a computer products and services firm.</p>
